<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- NowCastTab — the body of the NowCast window: watch boxes + storm-based warnings, and today's storm
     reports. One of three mode bodies (see Controls/Windows/TemporalWindow, registered once per mode); the
     window supplies the surface, the title and the pin, so this is content only.
     ⚠️ The file keeps its "Tab" name from when the three were tabs of one Timeframe window. It is the same
     control, unchanged by the split; renaming all three would be churn. Bound to the coordinator MapViewModel.

       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │  Radar ──────────────────────────────────────────    │
       │  Opacity ─────────●──                                │  ← sections run in the map's
       │  ────────────────────────────────────────────────    │     Z-ORDER: radar, then the
       │  Watches ────────────────────────────────────────    │     alerts over it, then the
       │  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │     reports on top
       │  │ 2 active watches                           │      │
       │  │ Updated 12:04 PM                           │      │  the same card + type rows in
       │  └────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │  all three overlay sections —
       │  [ ] ■ Tornado                             1         │  PhenomOverlayInput here,
       │  [ ] ■ Severe thunderstorm                 1         │  StormReportsInput below
       │  Opacity ──────●───────────                          │
       │  ────────────────────────────────────────────────    │
       │  Warnings ───────────────────────────────────────    │
       │  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
       │  │ 7 active warnings                          │      │
       │  │ Updated 12:04 PM · checking every 15s      │      │
       │  └────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │
       │  [ ] ■ Tornado                             0         │
       │  [x] ■ Severe thunderstorm                 7         │
       │  Opacity ──────●───────────                          │
       │  ────────────────────────────────────────────────    │
       │  Storm reports ──────────────────────────────────    │
       │  StormReportsInput  (today's reports)                │
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

     The body holds the "now"-oriented live-conditions options: the SPC Watch boxes and the storm-based
     Warning polygons (Tornado / Severe Thunderstorm). Both are active, event-driven current-conditions
     alerts, so they live under NowCast rather than ForeCast, in the UI and in the VM layer alike (their own
     WatchesViewModel / WarningsViewModel).

     ⚠️ THE WINDOW FOLLOWS PASTCAST'S SECTION GRAMMAR, deliberately: a Primitives/SectionHeading, then a
     summary CARD, then a rule, then the rows. It used to be headings over bare [label | control] grids with
     a local NowLabelStyle — character-for-character the shared SettingsFieldLabelStyle at a different
     width — which is most of why the two windows read as two different forms. Every row here is now a
     shared control or the shared label style. Add a section = a heading plus its control, in Z-order.

     ⚠️ WATCHES AND WARNINGS HAVE SEPARATE HEADINGS, which reverses an earlier decision (they shared one,
     "Watches and warnings", because they are one idea — current-conditions alerts). What changed is that
     each now carries its OWN card describing its OWN active set, and one heading cannot introduce two
     cards. They are also visually identical — the same two type rows, the same two colours — so the
     headings are the only thing telling you which is which.

     Both alert sections are the SAME control (Composites/PhenomOverlayInput) bound to a different view
     model, exactly as watches.js and warnings.js are the same JS factory with a different config. Storm
     reports stay their own control — the PastCast window shows that same block, so it is content of TWO
     hosts.

     ⚠️ This tab does NOT arm or clear NowCast; that is the NowCast key in the bottom bar's centre cluster.
     A tab body configures a mode, the key runs it. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.NowCastTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:comp="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <Grid VerticalAlignment="Top" RowSpacing="12">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the radar layer itself -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- divider -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- watches -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- divider -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- warnings -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- divider -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- storm reports (today) -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- ===================== RADAR: the layer everything else is drawn OVER ===================== -->
        <!-- ⚠️ Sections run in the map's Z-ORDER — radar underneath, watches, then warnings over those,
             reports on top. Same control and same ordering as the PastCast window; the value behind it is
             global, which is only safe because Past and Now are mutually exclusive modes and these two
             windows can never be open at once. -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- section heading -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the shared control -->
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <prim:SectionHeading Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,0,0,12" Text="Radar"/>
            <comp:RadarOverlayInput Grid.Row="1" ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Grid>

        <Border Grid.Row="1" Height="1" Margin="0,2"
                Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

        <!-- ===================== WATCHES: the large county-aggregated outlook areas ===================== -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="2">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- section heading -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the shared control -->
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <prim:SectionHeading Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,0,0,12" Text="Watches"/>
            <comp:PhenomOverlayInput Grid.Row="1" AlertNoun="watches"
                                     ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Watches, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Grid>

        <Border Grid.Row="3" Height="1" Margin="0,2"
                Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>

        <!-- ===================== WARNINGS: the imminent-threat polygons, drawn over the watches ========= -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="4">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- section heading -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the shared control -->
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <prim:SectionHeading Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,0,0,12" Text="Warnings"/>
            <comp:PhenomOverlayInput Grid.Row="1" AlertNoun="warnings"
                                     ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Warnings, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Grid>

        <Border Grid.Row="5" Height="1" Margin="0,2"
                Background="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
        <!-- ===================== STORM REPORTS ===================== -->
        <!-- ⚠️ The heading is HERE, not inside StormReportsInput: that control is shared by BOTH
             temporal windows, and a window owns its own section structure while the control is just
             content. Putting it inside would give this section a heading in a window whose other
             sections might not have one. (The same rule keeps the two headings above out of
             PhenomOverlayInput, which is shared between the two sections in THIS window.) -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="6">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- section heading -->
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the shared control -->
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <prim:SectionHeading Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,0,0,12" Text="Storm reports"/>
            <comp:StormReportsInput Grid.Row="1" ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
